Description: small editor for text, code, and LaTeX, with a browser and terminal
 minicode is a light, keyboard-first editor for text, code, and LaTeX. One
 window holds a file tree, an editor with syntax highlighting for about 200
 languages and file types, a terminal panel, a web browser panel, and a
 Source Control panel for staging, committing, and browsing the commit
 graph.
 .
 Markdown files open rendered, with tables, pictures, and links, and any
 block can be edited from the preview. Images, PDFs, video, and audio open
 in the editor's place. LaTeX files are typeset as you type and can be
 edited by double-clicking the page, using tectonic, which minicode
 offers to download when it is not installed. Completion, diagnostics, and
 go to definition come from language servers such as clangd, pylsp,
 gopls, and rust-analyzer when they are installed.
 .
 This is the GTK 4 build of the macOS app of the same name, sharing its
 C++ core.
